     \"column\": \"Validation Accuracy\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.0039972746340475665,\n        \"min\": 0.950742,\n        \"max\": 0.956395,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.950742,\n          0.956395\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Test Accuracy\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.0050919110353042545,\n        \"min\": 0.9447716107771641,\n        \"max\": 0.9519726604216886,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.9447716107771641,\n          0.9519726604216886\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Test Loss\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.001167267506221338,\n        \"min\": 0.18492598831653595,\n        \"max\": 0.1865767538547516,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.18492598831653595,\n          0.1865767538547516\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Training Time (min)\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 40.12876945174434,\n        \"min\": 68.58143666666666,\n        \"max\": 125.33208666666665,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          68.58143666666666,\n          125.33208666666665\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Samples/sec\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 1.9523218228560582,\n        \"min\": 3.336,\n        \"max\": 6.097,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          6.097,\n          3.336\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":5}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Task 3: Results and Analysis\n","\n","Partial freezing substantially reduced the number of parameters that needed to\n","be updated during fine-tuning. The baseline trained all 134,747,153 parameters,\n","whereas the partial-freezing model trained only 21,276,689 parameters, a\n","reduction of approximately 84.21%.\n","\n","This reduction was accompanied by a decrease in training time from approximately\n","125.3 minutes to 68.6 minutes, representing a reduction of about 45.28%.\n","Training throughput also increased from 3.34 to 6.10 samples per second.\n","\n","The efficiency improvement came with a modest reduction in POS-tagging\n","performance. Validation accuracy decreased from 95.64% to 95.07%, while test\n","accuracy decreased from 95.20% to 94.48%, a difference of 0.72 percentage\n","points on the test set.\n","\n","These results suggest that the upper three Transformer layers and the\n","classification head were able to adapt effectively to the POS-tagging task\n","despite the lower layers being frozen. However, the small reduction in accuracy\n","indicates that the frozen lower layers still provide representations that\n","contribute to task performance. Therefore, partial freezing produced a\n","clear efficiency benefit but did not completely preserve baseline accuracy.\n","\n","The experiment supports the use of partial freezing as a parameter-efficient\n","fine-tuning strategy, while also showing that the choice of which layers to\n","freeze can affect the accuracy-efficiency trade-off."],"metadata":{"id":"MM1PCCkEdowy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Layer Selection Rationale\n","\n","I froze the embedding layer and Transformer layers 0–2 while keeping layers\n","3–5 and the classification head trainable.\n","\n","The choice was based on the hypothesis that lower layers capture more general\n","subword and contextual representations, while higher layers are more\n","specialized and therefore more useful for adapting the pretrained model to a\n","specific downstream task such as POS tagging.\n","\n","This was treated as an experimental hypothesis rather than an assumption that\n","the lower layers are unimportant. The results allow the effect of this\n","specific freezing configuration to be evaluated empirically."],"metadata":{"id":"8-VzqE0Jd04e"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[" Limitations\n","\n","This experiment evaluates only one partial-freezing configuration: freezing\n","the embeddings and the first three Transformer layers. Other configurations,\n","such as freezing fewer or more layers, could produce different\n","accuracy-efficiency trade-offs.\n","\n","The experiment also uses English-EWT rather than Yorùbá because the official\n","Yorùbá-YTB repository available for this task did not provide the required\n","training and development splits. The official Yorùbá test data was therefore\n","not split into training data, and English-EWT was used to maintain a valid\n","train/development/test evaluation setup.\n","\n","Finally, evaluation accuracy is calculated over the non-ignored subword\n","tokens after label alignment. Thus, it should not be interpreted as strictly\n","word-level POS accuracy."],"metadata":{"id":"8TyR1xPGd3JW"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[" Proposed Extensions\n","\n","Several extensions could be investigated:\n","\n","1. Different freezing depths: compare freezing 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5\n","   Transformer layers to identify a better accuracy-efficiency trade-off.\n","\n","2. Layer-wise POS analysis: examine which POS categories are most affected\n","   by different freezing configurations.\n","\n","3. Language-specific evaluation: repeat the experiment on a UD treebank\n","   with different linguistic characteristics, including a low-resource\n","   language, to determine whether the observed efficiency-accuracy trade-off\n","   generalizes across languages."],"metadata":{"id":"eHQ_Ure2d8w2"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Conclusion\n","\n","The experiment shows that partial freezing can substantially reduce the\n","computational cost of POS-tagging fine-tuning. Freezing the embeddings and\n","first three Transformer layers reduced the number of trainable parameters by\n","84.21% and training time by approximately 45%, while reducing test accuracy\n","by 0.72 percentage points.\n","\n","The results demonstrate that a large proportion of the model can remain frozen\n","while the upper layers adapt to the downstream task. At the same time, the\n","accuracy difference indicates that freezing decisions matter and should be\n","validated experimentally rather than assumed to be universally optimal."],"metadata":{"id":"68_M3Y_-eLgQ"}}]}